From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] AP: fix STA state after unacknowledged association response

When the driver reports no ACK for a (Re)Association Response with
status SUCCESS, hostapd removes the STA from the kernel driver but
keeps its own STA entry. Three problems with that:

1. The TX status may be stale. With full AP client state, a new
   authentication exchange re-adds the driver STA entry through
   ap_sta_re_add() while the TX status of the previous association
   attempt can still be pending in the driver (e.g. flushed as
   "no ACK" by the STA removal itself on mt76). Processing that
   stale callback removed the just re-added driver entry, and the
   following association failed NL80211_CMD_SET_STATION with
   -ENOENT ("Could not set STA to kernel driver"), repeating on
   every retry cycle. add_associated_sta() clears added_unassoc
   before the response frame is sent, so a genuine TX status for
   the current attempt always sees added_unassoc == 0; skip the
   removal when it is still set.

2. The WPA state machine was not notified about the removal, so
   tk_already_set stayed true for FT/FILS. A later FT or FILS
   reassociation then kept using set-STA on a driver entry that no
   longer existed and could never recover. Send WPA_DRV_STA_REMOVED
   like add_associated_sta() does, so the next reassociation takes
   the remove+add path and reinstalls the TK. The driver entry and
   its keys are already gone at this point, so this does not enable
   TK reinstallation against a live key.

3. The authorized state survived the removal. A previously
   authorized STA retrying after the unacknowledged response was
   re-added to the driver with WLAN_STA_AUTHORIZED already set,
   before the new exchange completed. Clear the authorized state
   next to the removal, matching what ap_sta_re_add() does.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
@@ -8635,9 +8635,30 @@ static void handle_assoc_cb(struct hosta
 			       HOSTAPD_LEVEL_DEBUG,
 			       "did not acknowledge association response");
 		sta->flags &= ~WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK;
-		/* The STA is added only in case of SUCCESS */
-		if (status == WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS)
+		/* The STA is added only in case of SUCCESS.
+		 *
+		 * Skip the removal if the STA has already been re-added for a
+		 * newer authentication exchange; the TX status is stale in
+		 * that case and the driver STA entry belongs to the new
+		 * exchange. add_associated_sta() clears added_unassoc before
+		 * the response is sent, so a TX status for this response
+		 * always sees added_unassoc == 0.
+		 *
+		 * Notify the WPA state machine about the removal so that a
+		 * previously installed TK is not considered valid anymore.
+		 * Without this, a following FT/FILS reassociation would keep
+		 * using set-STA on a driver entry that no longer exists and
+		 * the STA could never reconnect until a fresh authentication
+		 * clears the state.
+		 *
+		 * Clear the authorized state as well; otherwise the retry
+		 * would re-add the driver entry with the authorized flag
+		 * already set before the new exchange has completed. */
+		if (status == WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS && !sta->added_unassoc) {
+			ap_sta_set_authorized(hapd, sta, 0);
 			hostapd_drv_sta_remove(hapd, sta->addr);
+			wpa_auth_sm_event(sta->wpa_sm, WPA_DRV_STA_REMOVED);
+		}
 
 		goto handle_ml;
 	}
